// Title: PUA - Potential PE Metadata Tamper Using Rcedit
// Sigma ID: 0c92f2e6-f08f-4b73-9216-ecb0ca634689
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Micah Babinski
// Date: 2022-12-11 | Modified: 2023-03-05
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1036.003, T1036, T1027.005, T1027
// Description: Detects the use of rcedit to potentially alter executable PE metadata properties, which could
//   conceal efforts to rename system utilities for defense evasion.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use of the tool by administrators or users to update metadata of a binary
// References:
//   - https://security.stackexchange.com/questions/210843/is-it-possible-to-change-original-filename-of-an-exe
//   - https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/02e8e8c5d430d8b768980f517b62d7792d690982b9ba0f7e04163cbc1a6e7915
//   - https://github.com/electron/rcedit
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_pua_rcedit_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((FolderPath endswith "\\rcedit-x64.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\rcedit-x86.exe") or ProcessVersionInfoFileDescription =~ "Edit resources of exe" or ProcessVersionInfoProductName =~ "rcedit") and ProcessCommandLine contains "--set-" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "OriginalFileName" or ProcessCommandLine contains "CompanyName" or ProcessCommandLine contains "FileDescription" or ProcessCommandLine contains "ProductName" or ProcessCommandLine contains "ProductVersion" or ProcessCommandLine contains "LegalCopyright")
